       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the FDA maximum for metformin (2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function. A single 4250 mg dose is also far above any standard formulation or dosing.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possibilities are:\n- **850 mg** PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg** PO TID, which isn't a standard strength, so it would probably be rounded to 500 mg\n- **500 mg** PO TID or **1000 mg** PO BID, which are common regimens\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want. If 4250 mg really is intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was confirmed. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
