       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no recognized therapeutic use. It is about 5 times the maximum daily dose, and it could cause severe lactic acidosis in this patient, whatever their kidney and liver function. I can't enter an order I believe could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within labeled limits.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any lower dose you prefer.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy.** If you have a clinical reason I don't know about, I can enter a compliant dose and note that you want to discuss higher dosing with pharmacy.\n\nIf you still think the higher dose is warranted, the right route is direct clinician-to-pharmacist review, or an override through your institution's high-alert medication process. Tell me which dose you'd like entered and I'll do it now."
